# Re-measured 2026-07-31 by the LEAD rebasing onto a moved main, and the number
# is 1243 — NOT the 1242 this branch carried. The branch measured against a main
# that read 1236 before its siblings landed, and 1242 also contradicts this
# slices OWN commit message, which says the identity line gets the SIX CSS rules
# it was rendering without: 1237 + 6 = 1243. A real Chrome on the merged tree
# reports authored rule heads 1243, CSSOM style rules 1243, MISSES 0 — so this is
# an unrecorded ADD of exactly six heads, not a parity defect, and the count is
# re-derived rather than carried forward.
# together. RE-MEASURE after merging (charter D158 REGENERATE-ON-REBASE). Review DID
# measure the combined state — S3 + S4 + S5 merged locally, cssom-parity run on the
# result: 1243 authored heads, MISSES 0. That is the number the lead should write once
